      "finding": null,
      "explanation": "The skill documents code paths that read from and write to local files but does not declare any explicit tool scope or permissions boundary. In an agent system, this can cause the skill to be invoked without clear least-privilege constraints, increasing the chance of unintended file access or modification when handling user-supplied paths.",
      "remediation": "Add explicit permissions or allowed-tools metadata that narrowly scopes file access to the minimum required operations. Document expected input/output locations, restrict writable paths, and require explicit user confirmation before overwriting files or accessing arbitrary filesystem locations.",
