    {
      "id": "TP4",
      "finding_id": "finding-02601a12de4c474c998b2914d2e4ff14",
      "category": "MCP Tool Poisoning",
      "pattern": null,
      "severity": "HIGH",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "location": {
        "file": "SKILL.md",
        "start_line": 1,
        "end_line": null
      },
      "finding": null,
      "explanation": "This is a mismatch because the declared description presents the skill as a comprehensive, general PDF utility to use whenever the user wants 'anything with PDF files.' The actual code does not implement that broad scope. Instead, it is specialized for PDF form handling: checking whether a PDF has fillable fields, extracting form field info, extracting rough structure from non-fillable forms, converting PDF pages to images, validating bounding boxes, drawing validation overlays, and filling forms either through native fields or text annotations. There is no implementation for merging, splitting, rotating, watermarking, encryption/decryption, OCR, or broad PDF creation. The trigger guidance is also overly broad relative to the code, because 'anything with PDF files' would activate this skill for many unrelated PDF tasks it cannot perform. While some listed capabilities loosely overlap (image extraction via page rasterization, limited text extraction for form labels, and form filling), the overall declared purpose materially overstates and mischaracterizes the skill's real behavior.",
      "remediation": "Update the skill description to accurately reflect all capabilities, or remove undeclared functionality from the implementation.",
      "code_snippet": null,
      "intent": null,
      "tags": [
        "ASI02",
        "AML.T0080",
        "llm-unconfirmed"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "SQP-1",
      "finding_id": "finding-e94d86494f114030959f8f099a4bc4eb",
      "category": null,
      "pattern": null,
      "severity": "HIGH",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "location": {
        "file": "SKILL.md",
        "start_line": 3,
        "end_line": 3
      },
      "finding": null,
      "explanation": "The activation text is extremely broad ('whenever the user wants to do anything with PDF files' and any mention of a .pdf), which can cause over-triggering on routine conversations and route unrelated or minimally related tasks into a file-manipulating skill. In an agentic environment, overly eager activation expands the attack surface by increasing opportunities for unnecessary file reads, writes, OCR, or command usage on untrusted documents.",
      "remediation": "Narrow the activation criteria to specific user intents such as extract text, merge PDFs, OCR scanned documents, or fill forms. Avoid trigger language based solely on file extension mentions, and require clear task intent plus user authorization before performing file or command-line operations.",
      "code_snippet": null,
      "intent": null,
      "tags": []
    },
    {
      "id": "SQP-2",
      "finding_id": "finding-b4eb0c56838a4444a206b834f028b471",
