        "end_line": 586
      },
      "finding": null,
      "explanation": "The example `qpdf --replace-input corrupted.pdf` performs an in-place modification of the original file without any warning, backup step, or safer alternative. In a PDF-processing skill, users are likely to copy commands verbatim, so this can cause accidental data loss or irreversible alteration of important documents, especially when working on damaged files that may need preservation for recovery.",
      "remediation": "Replace the in-place example with a non-destructive workflow, such as writing to a separate output file (for example, repair to `repaired.pdf`) and only overwriting after validation. Add an explicit warning wherever destructive flags like `--replace-input` are shown, and prefer examples that preserve the original file by default.",
      "code_snippet": null,
      "intent": null,
      "tags": []
    }
